{"url": "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/events.cfm", "final_url": "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/events.cfm", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "Skip to main content\nShow\nMenu\nUNIVERSITY ANNOUNCEMENT\nNotice for AU employees: Learn More\nYou are here:\nAmerican University\nCollege of Arts & Sciences\nCAS Admissions\nEvents & Visits\nGraduate Admissions Home\nDegrees & Programs\nHow to Apply\nEvents & Visits for Prospective Students\nRequirements & Deadlines\nInternational Applicants\nTuition, Funding & Scholarships\nPartnerships\nStaff\nFor Admitted Students\nCONTACT US\n202-885-3620\ncasgrad@american.edu\nMonday-Friday, 9:00-5:00; please allow 1 business day for responses.\nBattelle Tompkins, Room T-21\non a map\nCAS-Graduate Admissions\n4400 Massachusetts Avenue NW\nWashington, DC 20016-8081 United States\nCollege of Arts and Sciences on Facebook\nCollege of Arts and Sciences on Youtube\nCollege of Arts and Sciences on LinkedIn\nCollege of Arts and Sciences on Instagram\nEvents & Visits\nFor Prospective Students\nThe College of Arts and Sciences offers visitors a number of ways to connect with us and explore all that we have to offer. New events on campus or online, as well as regional events, are added throughout the year, so please check back for options as they emerge. Please browse below or use the jump links for upcoming events and ways to visit:\nOnline Events\nVirtual Visits\nOn-Campus Tours\nOnline Events\nNext Online Events\nAdmission Fundamentals, Nov. 13, 12:00\u20131:00\nStatistics Ask-Me-Anything, Nov. 16, 12:00\u20131:00\nGrad School Planning, Nov. 20, 12:00\u20131:00\nStatistics Ask-Me-Anything, Nov. 23, 12:00\u20131:00\nStatistics Ask-Me-Anything, Nov. 30, 12:00\u20131:00\nGrad School Planning, Dec. 4, 12:00\u20131:00\nAdmission Fundamentals, Dec. 11, 12:00\u20131:00\nGrad School Planning, Dec. 18, 12:00\u20131:00\nAll Grad Admissions Events\nAll Degree Program Spotlights\nDrop-In Admissions Advising\nVirtual Visits with Graduate Advisors\nAdmission advisors are available for virtual visits using the Zoom platform. While it is best to speak with the representative who works with your intended program, any staff member can assist you with questions regarding our graduate programs and the application process.\nMeet with Laurel Semple\nSchedule a Virtual Meeting with Laurel, or contact her (semple@american.edu) for admissions questions about these CAS programs:\nAnthropology\nArt History\nBiomedical & Environmental Sciences (PhD)\nCreative Writing\nEconomics\nEnvironmental Science\nEthics, Peace & Human Rights\nHistory\nLiterature\nPhilosophy\nPostbaccalaureate Pre-Medical Certificate\nSociology\nStudio Art\nTranslation Certificate (French, German, Russian, Spanish)\nMeet with Hallie Tingstad\nSchedule a Virtual Meeting with Hallie, or contact her (hallie@american.edu) for admissions questions about these CAS programs:\nAudio Technology\nBehavior, Cognition, Neuroscience (PhD)\nClinical Psychology (PhD, MA)\nComputer Science\nData Science (campus or online)\nHealth Promotion (campus or online)\nNutrition Education (online)\nPsychology\nPublic Health, Innovation & Practice\nStatistics\nOn-Campus Visits\nFor applicants who wish to visit campus, we offer in-person meetings with an admissions ambassador. This can include a campus tour (take a virtual campus preview) and faculty visit, contingent on availability. Meeting details and parking instructions are emailed the week of the visit. Please provide at least one week's notice for all requests. Please email casgrad@american.edu to arrange an on-campus visit \u2014 or join a scheduled campus tour.\nNovember 13, 2:00\nNovember 20, 2:00\nDecember 4, 2:00\nDecember 11, 2:00\n4400 Massachusetts Avenue, NW\nWashington, DC 20016\n(202) 885-1000\nContact Us\nVisit AU\nWork at AU\nCookie Preferences\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 American University.\nEmergency Preparedness\nPolicies\nPrivacy\nDisclosure\nEEO\nTitle IX\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYoutube\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nHomepage\nBy clicking \u201cAccept All Cookies\u201d, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Privacy Notice\nCookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/events.cfm#emergency-top"], ["", "https://www.american.edu/"], ["Search", "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/events.cfm#new-search"], ["Browse Departments & Services", "https://www.american.edu/directory/?d=departments"], ["Log in", "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/events.cfm#login-detail-new"], ["myAU Portal", "https://myau.american.edu/"], ["Email", "https://mail.american.edu"], ["Canvas", "https://canvas.american.edu/"], ["Admissions & Aid", "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/events.cfm#mainmenu-1"], ["Undergraduate Admissions", "https://www.american.edu/admissions/index.cfm"], ["Graduate Admissions", "https://www.american.edu/admissions/graduate-admissions/index.cfm"], ["Tuition & Fees", "https://www.american.edu/finance/studentaccounts/Tuition-and-Fees-Information.cfm"], ["Financial Aid", "https://www.american.edu/financialaid/index.cfm"], ["Academics", "https://www.american.edu/cas/admissions/events.cfm#mainmenu-8"], ["Academics Home", "https://www.american.edu/academics/index.cfm"], ["Degrees", "https://www.american.edu/programs/"], ["Registration", "https://www.american.edu/provost/registrar/studentservices/registration.cfm"], ["Schedule of Classes", "https://www.american.edu/provost/registrar/schedule/"], ["Study Abroad", "http://auabroad.american.edu"], ["Summer Programs", "https://www.american.edu/summer/index.cfm"], ["Online Programs", "https://www.american.edu/onlinelearning/index.cfm"], ["Honors & Learning Communities", "https://www.american.edu/learning-communities/index.cfm"], ["Professional & Lifelong Learning", "https://www.american.edu/professional-and-lifelo